          },
          "version": 0.941
        },
        "actionType": {
          "value": "passive"
        },
        "actions": {
          "value": null
        },
        "category": null,
        "deathNote": false,
        "description": {
          "gm": "",
          "value": "<p>When the Lord of Gears hits a target with its grappling hook, it can choose to use a second action to pull itself to the target instead of pulling the target towards it, as long as the target is within the first range increment. The targeted creature must succeed on a @Check[type:reflex|dc:37|basic:true] save or take Fist Strike damage as the Lord of Gears slams into them. This movement does not trigger reactions.</p><p>This can move through creatures, but cannot end in the same space as one. The Lord of Gears can choose which space it ends up in around its target. For the purposes of multi-attack penalty, this counts as a normal Grappling Hook attack (and so still doesn't increase the penalty until after a follow-up Hydraulic Punch).</p>"
        },
        "publication": {
          "authors": "",
          "license": "OGL",
